#!/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/bash
set -e

# The commands (adb-connect, shizuku-watchdog, shizuku-pair, shizuku-setup)
# are installed by dpkg into $PREFIX/bin straight from the package
# payload; nothing user-facing goes to ~/.local/bin. Only the Termux:Boot
# launchers must live in $HOME, so just those two are staged under
# $PREFIX/opt and copied here (the only legitimate $HOME exception).
#
# The interactive setup runs only when a terminal is attached. Without one
# (unattended install) the services start with the current or default
# configuration and the user is told to run shizuku-setup.

PREFIX="/data/data/com.termux/files/usr"
SRC="$PREFIX/opt/shizuku-semi-auto"
DEST_HOME="/data/data/com.termux/files/home"

mkdir -p "$DEST_HOME/.local/tmp" "$DEST_HOME/.termux/boot"

cp "$SRC/boot/adb-connect"      "$DEST_HOME/.termux/boot/adb-connect"
cp "$SRC/boot/shizuku-watchdog" "$DEST_HOME/.termux/boot/shizuku-watchdog"

chmod +x "$DEST_HOME/.termux/boot/adb-connect" "$DEST_HOME/.termux/boot/shizuku-watchdog"

# adb has to run before anything else makes sense.
ADB_OK=1
if ! "$PREFIX/bin/adb" version >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    ADB_OK=0
fi

cat <<'MSG'

== shizuku-semi-auto installed ==

Commands are in $PREFIX/bin (already in PATH):
  shizuku-setup   interactive configuration (run it again any time)
  shizuku-pair    guided pairing / manual connection (Android 11+)
  adb-connect, shizuku-watchdog   background services, started at boot

Requirements:
1) Termux:Boot installed and OPENED at least once. IMPORTANT: it must
   come from the SAME source as your main Termux app (GitHub or
   F-Droid, not mixed) - Android refuses to run apps that share
   Termux's signature scope if they are signed with different keys.
   Check your current app's source with: echo $TERMUX_APK_RELEASE
2) Shizuku app installed. On versions before 13.6: open its "ADB" tab
   once so it generates start.sh (13.6+ uses libshizuku.so instead).
3) Optional: pkg install -y termux-api + the Termux:API app (same
   source as above), for status notifications and, on Android 11+,
   for reading the Wireless debugging port from a notification.

Modes:
- Wireless (Android 11+): pair once; after that the services reconnect
  by themselves at every boot while Wireless debugging is on and its
  port can be read (recommended notification app: KeepADB, package
  de.hohnepeople.keepadb).
- Cable (any version): after boot, run 'adb tcpip 5555' from a second
  device or a PC; adb-connect detects it within a second.

IMPORTANT - USB priming: it exists because of a freeze diagnosed on a
specific device/ROM (unplugging the cable without a real USB-mode
transition left the ADB-over-network shell unresponsive). There is NO
guarantee the bug exists on another device. By default it runs only in
cable mode and puts your USB mode back afterwards. Change it with
shizuku-setup (auto / on / off).

Logs: ~/.local/tmp/*.log

---

== shizuku-semi-auto instalado ==

Los comandos están en $PREFIX/bin (ya en el PATH):
  shizuku-setup   configuración interactiva (puedes repetirla cuando quieras)
  shizuku-pair    emparejamiento guiado / conexión manual (Android 11+)
  adb-connect, shizuku-watchdog   servicios en segundo plano, se inician al arrancar

Requisitos:
1) Termux:Boot instalada y ABIERTA al menos una vez. IMPORTANTE: debe
   venir de la MISMA fuente que tu app principal de Termux (GitHub o
   F-Droid, sin mezclar): Android se niega a ejecutar apps que
   comparten el alcance de firma de Termux si están firmadas con
   claves distintas. Comprueba la fuente de tu app con:
   echo $TERMUX_APK_RELEASE
2) App Shizuku instalada. En versiones anteriores a 13.6: abre una vez
   su pestaña "ADB" para que genere start.sh (13.6+ usa libshizuku.so).
3) Opcional: pkg install -y termux-api + la app Termux:API (misma
   fuente que arriba), para las notificaciones de estado y, en
   Android 11+, para leer el puerto de la depuración inalámbrica desde
   una notificación.

Modos:
- Inalámbrico (Android 11+): se empareja una vez; después los servicios
  se reconectan solos en cada arranque mientras la depuración
  inalámbrica esté activa y su puerto se pueda leer (app de
  notificación recomendada: KeepADB, paquete de.hohnepeople.keepadb).
- Cable (cualquier versión): tras el arranque, ejecuta 'adb tcpip 5555'
  desde un segundo equipo o un PC; adb-connect lo detecta en un segundo.

IMPORTANTE - priming USB: existe por un cuelgue diagnosticado en un
dispositivo/ROM concreto (desconectar el cable sin una transición real
de modo USB dejaba sin respuesta el shell ADB por red). NO hay garantía
de que el fallo exista en otro equipo. Por defecto solo se ejecuta en
modo cable y devuelve tu modo USB al terminar. Cámbialo con
shizuku-setup (auto / on / off).

Registros: ~/.local/tmp/*.log
MSG

if [ "$ADB_OK" -ne 1 ]; then
    cat <<'WARN'

!! PROBLEM: 'adb' is installed but does not run ('CANNOT LINK EXECUTABLE
   ... cannot locate symbol ...' = your libc++ is older than the
   android-tools build).
   FIX:
     pkg update && pkg upgrade -y
     pkg reinstall android-tools
   If it persists, your Termux install may mix F-Droid and GitHub
   builds - reinstall all Termux apps from ONE source.

---

!! PROBLEMA: 'adb' está instalado pero no se ejecuta ('CANNOT LINK
   EXECUTABLE ... cannot locate symbol ...' = tu libc++ es más antigua
   que el build de android-tools).
   ARREGLO:
     pkg update && pkg upgrade -y
     pkg reinstall android-tools
   Si persiste, tu instalación de Termux puede mezclar builds de F-Droid
   y GitHub: reinstala todas las apps de Termux desde UNA sola fuente.
WARN
fi

if [ -t 0 ]; then
    "$PREFIX/bin/shizuku-setup" --postinst || true
else
    "$PREFIX/bin/shizuku-setup" --start || true
    echo
    echo "No terminal attached: services started with the current/default configuration."
    echo "Run 'shizuku-setup' to configure them. / Ejecuta 'shizuku-setup' para configurarlos."
fi
